 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** O(1) per pixel per frame for the RLS update, as it involves fixed-size matrix-vector operations (assuming fixed $d$). The spatial filtering step is O(N) where N is the number of pixels, with a constant factor depending on the window size (e.g., $5 \times 5$) [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** O(N) per pixel, storing $\beta_j$, $P_j$, and $z_j$ [S1].
-*   **Measured Performance:** The method is designed for real-time VPT. It reduces spike noise and maintains temporal stability better than standard RLS in low-sample scenarios [S1].
